From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:41:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042_battery: wait out the alert after a
 failed read too

The MAX77759 sleep added at the end of max17042_thread_handler() is
skipped when the Status read fails: the handler returns early, the
oneshot interrupt is unmasked while ALRT is still asserted, and an I2C
error during an alert would burst as before. Move the sleep to a common
exit, so both paths wait one task period.

Tested on a Pixel 7 (7.3.0-rc6), with only this change on top of the
kernel it ran before: with the cable out for 15 minutes, seven alerts
(RepSOC reaching 99 % on the cable, then six steps down to 93 %) fired
the gauge's interrupt once each, as before this change, and the gauge
read as before. The failed-read path itself wasn't triggered.

Suggested-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index e40540228..7c6ea8e6d 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -1224,7 +1224,7 @@ static irqreturn_t max17042_thread_handler(int id, void *dev)
 
 	ret = regmap_read(chip->regmap, MAX17042_STATUS, &val);
 	if (ret)
-		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+		goto out;
 
 	if ((val & STATUS_SMN_BIT) || (val & STATUS_SMX_BIT) ||
 	    (val & STATUS_DSOCI_BIT)) {
@@ -1238,11 +1238,13 @@ static irqreturn_t max17042_thread_handler(int id, void *dev)
 
 	power_supply_changed(chip->battery);
 
+out:
 	/*
 	 * The MAX77759 releases ALRT only at its next task period after
 	 * Status is cleared, so the level interrupt would fire again as soon
 	 * as the oneshot thread returns, hundreds of times per alert. Wait
-	 * one task period (in units of 1/32768 s) before returning.
+	 * one task period (in units of 1/32768 s) before returning, also
+	 * after a failed Status read.
 	 */
 	if (chip->chip_type == MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX77759)
 		msleep(DIV_ROUND_UP(chip->task_period * MSEC_PER_SEC, 32768));
